200: **READ: A separate `xmem` address-operand aliasing defect is visible in the source.** The load receives live pointers to the destination and address-source registers. It updates the destination before the store, while the store reuses the address-source pointers and recomputes its effective address. If the destination overlaps an address-source register, that computation can therefore change between the two halves. See [xmem_slow](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c:2385) and the [load/store address computation](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:248).
