130: ## Q4 -- else found
131: 
132: `M88K_PSR_BO` is set only at `cpu_m88k.c:182-183`, and at that moment `:130` has just assigned big-endian, so the bit stays clear. The file loader and the config override later change `cpu->byte_order` and do not touch the PSR. The generic load/store path sets `DMT_BO` from `cpu->byte_order` (`cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:111-112`). `ldcr` of a DMT then stops the CPU when that bit disagrees with the PSR (`cpu_m88k.c:472-477`). The table index still follows `cpu->byte_order`, and the fast byte path never writes the DMT, so P1's reachability stands. The PSR disagreement is a separate little-endian footgun, outside this round.

