513: ~~~~
514: `kind` is the table axis: `ld.bu` = unsigned load (the slot `xmem`'s load half uses), `ld.b` = signed load, `st.b` =
515: store.  The 12 distinct names are the right-hand column with the `[index]` dropped.
516: 
517: The script (`table_census.py`, in the drafter's scratchpad, not in the repository):
518: ~~~~
519: import re, sys
520: src = open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8").read()
521: start = src.index("m88k_loadstore[512]")
522: body = src[src.index("{", start)+1 : src.index("};", start)]
523: ents = [e.strip() for e in body.split(",")]
524: ents = [e for e in ents if e]
525: print("entries parsed:", len(ents))
526: def fields(i):
527:     return dict(size=i&3, store=bool(i&4), signed=bool(i&8), be=bool(i&16), scaled=bool(i&32),
528:                 usr=bool(i&64), regofs=bool(i&128), nopcsync=bool(i&256))
529: nulls = [i for i,e in enumerate(ents) if e == "NULL"]
530: print("NULL entries:", len(nulls))
531: # classify NULLs by which generator arm (first match, in table-printer order)
532: def arm(i):
533:     f = fields(i)
534:     if f["store"] and f["signed"]: return "A store&&signedness"
535:     if (not f["regofs"]) and f["usr"]: return "B !regofs&&usr"
536:     if (not f["regofs"]) and f["scaled"]: return "C !regofs&&scaled"
537:     if f["size"] == 0 and f["scaled"]: return "D size==0&&scaled"
538:     return "none"
539: from collections import Counter
540: print("NULLs by arm:", dict(Counter(arm(i) for i in nulls)))
541: print("non-NULL entries with an arm (should be 0):", sum(1 for i,e in enumerate(ents) if e!="NULL" and arm(i)!="none"))
542: D = [i for i in nulls if arm(i) == "D size==0&&scaled"]
543: print("arm-D indices (%d):" % len(D), D)
544: print()
545: print("%-5s %-6s %-6s %-3s %-4s %-8s | slot   | unscaled counterpart (index-32)" % ("idx","kind","endian","usr","sync","",))
546: for i in D:
547:     f = fields(i)
548:     kind = "st.b" if f["store"] else ("ld.b" if f["signed"] else "ld.bu")
549:     cp = ents[i-32]
550:     print("%-5d %-6s %-6s %-3s %-4s          | %-6s | [%d] %s" % (i, kind, "BE" if f["be"] else "LE", "usr" if f["usr"] else "-", "nosync" if f["nopcsync"] else "sync", ents[i], i-32, cp))
551: ~~~~
552: 
553: **Producer enumeration -- which of the 24 slots a guest instruction can reach today.**  This is the drafter's reading
554: of the four producers in S10.  ENUMERATE IT YOURSELF; do not ratify it.
555: 
556: | slot(s) | cell | producer at HEAD |
557: |---|---|---|
558: | 176, 184, 180 | `ld.bu` / `ld.b` / `st.b`; big-endian; plain; PC-sync | the register-form `ld`/`st` decoder with its `scaled` set (:3622-3629) -> `ic->f == NULL` -> CPU stop (S6) |
559: | 240, 248, 244 | the same with `.usr` (the decoder's `user`, from `0x100`) | the same decoder path with `user` also set -> CPU stop |
560: | 432, 436 | `ld.bu` / `st.b`; big-endian; plain; no-PC-sync | `xmem_slow`'s load half (:2377-2382), then its store half (:2411-2417), when the handler's own `scaled` is set and `size` is clear -> NULL call -> process ends (S3) |
561: | 440, 504 | `ld.b`; big-endian; no-PC-sync; plain / `.usr` | none (P3) |
562: | 496, 500 | `ld.bu` / `st.b`; big-endian; `.usr`; no-PC-sync | none today; `xmem` becomes their producer if N2 is fixed (P2) |
563: | 160, 168, 164, 224, 232, 228, 416, 420 | the little-endian twins of the eight reachable cells above | the same producers, only if the CPU's byte order is little-endian (P1) |
564: | 424, 488, 480, 484 | the little-endian twins of 440, 504, 496, 500 | none (P1 with P2/P3) |
